The void tilts.  
A single card drifts down and hovers before your eyes.  
Gold borders catch light that is not there, and the card turns: **Temperance**.  
A calm warmth spreads through your chest, as if someone poured cool water on a fever you did not know you had.

A second card slides beside the first.  
Flames race across its face, then settle into the bold shape of the **Ace of Wands**.  
Heat prickles your fingertips; you smell sulfur and fresh-cut pine.

The third card flips without warning.  
A figure juggles twin coins caught in an endless loop—**Two of Pentacles**.  
Your pulse steadies, matching the quiet rhythm of the looping coins.

These cards are now yours. They hum in your memory.

The void shreds like burned silk.  
Floorboards take shape beneath your boots, and the scent of woodsmoke replaces the sulfur.  
You stand inside the Broken Lantern Inn, Ardent Hollow’s low ceiling pressing close, while the night outside keeps its own unsafe time.

